The restorer (src/restore.cpp) computes Apollo, the band-sequence audio
restoration network by Kai Li and Yi Luo (Tsinghua University and Tencent
AI Lab; "Apollo: Band-sequence Modeling for High-Quality Audio
Restoration", arXiv:2409.08514), from its published weights:

    huggingface.co/JusperLee/Apollo, pytorch_model.bin
    at commit c68bd80fdd9c0d93d2f4a833cb154624f660a561

The weights are released under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International License, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
(the full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode).

tenfold carries them modified: extras/apollo.tfq (apollo.tfq in the
packages) is the same weights with each convolution's kept more coarsely,
as whole multiples of a step per output channel, at the bits per layer in
extras/apollo-bits.txt (`tenfold restore-model` makes it from the
published file). That modified file is likewise licensed under CC BY-SA
4.0, with the attribution above.

tenfold's own code, the C++ that reads, compacts and runs the weights, is
written from the paper and the shapes of the weights, and is under
tenfold's licence (LICENSE).
